cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Edge DFIR Toolkit"
message: "If you use this toolkit or its platform catalog in research or published work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: DePalma
    given-names: Raymond
repository-code: "https://github.com/depalmar/edge-dfir-toolkit"
abstract: >-
  Forensic triage for compromised edge network devices - VPN concentrators,
  firewalls and gateways. Declarative per-vendor collection profiles run in
  order of volatility through restricted vendor CLIs with a read-only guard;
  vendor exports are ingested into a hash-chained case; per-CVE detection packs
  are scored with explicit evidence gaps. Ships a machine-readable platform
  catalog and vendor-neutral Sigma and YARA rules.
keywords:
  - digital forensics
  - incident response
  - DFIR
  - edge devices
  - VPN
  - firewall
  - detection engineering
  - triage
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: "2026-10-22"
